{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 30, :comments ["<b>It is a netek.</b> So is the name of the affliction 'netek' (נתק) because the hair was uprooted (נתק) from that place, in the language of our Rabbis of blessed memory: לאו שנתק לעשה — 'a prohibition uprooted becomes a positive command'; and likewise it is written (Joshua 4:18): נתקו כפות — 'the soles were lifted.' And after the original hair, which is natural, has been uprooted from there, if this thin yellow diseased hair grows there, behold it is a sign of impurity. Now the netek defiles by yellow hair and by spreading, and black hair is a sign of purity, for thus it is written: ושער שחור צמח בו נרפא הנתק טהור הוא וטהרו הכהן — 'and black hair has grown in it, the netek is healed, it is pure, and the priest shall pronounce it pure.'"], :book :leviticus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:25:14.594188545Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}